    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0651" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18437</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Johnson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brownsville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 15, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>About sixty bandits crossed the river about forty miles below Laredo at San
                    Ygnacio and attacked a part of our troops, killing three and wounding seven, one
                    of whom since died. Eight Mexicans were killed and don’t know how many wounded.
                    General Ricaut is afraid that if the Americans cross the river there will be
                    serious trouble, for one thousand Mexican soldiers have been sent to the border
                    to suppress the raiders and if the Americans cross river there will be a general
                    engagement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
